### Codegen Configuration with Custom Type Mappers

Source: https://github.com/dotansimha/graphql-code-generator/blob/master/website/src/pages/plugins/typescript/typescript-resolvers.mdx

Configure `graphql-codegen` to map GraphQL types to your custom model types using the `mappers` option. This allows you to use your own defined types for resolvers and context.

```typescript
import type { CodegenConfig } from '@graphql-codegen/cli'

const config: CodegenConfig = {
  schema: 'schema.graphql',
  generates: {
    './resolvers-types.ts': {
      config: {
        contextType: 'models#MyContextType',
        mappers: {
          User: './models#UserModel',
          Profile: './models#UserProfile'
        }
      },
      plugins: ['typescript', 'typescript-resolvers']
    }
  }
}
```

--------------------------------

### Configure Enum Mapping in codegen.ts

Source: https://github.com/dotansimha/graphql-code-generator/blob/master/website/src/pages/plugins/typescript/typescript-resolvers.mdx

Maps a GraphQL enum to a specific TypeScript enum export.

```typescript
import type { CodegenConfig } from '@graphql-codegen/cli'

const config: CodegenConfig = {
  schema: 'schema.graphql',
  generates: {
    './resolvers-types.ts': {
      config: {
        enumValues: {
          Color: './enums#ColorsCode'
        }
      },
      plugins: ['typescript', 'typescript-resolvers']
    }
  }
}
export default config
```

--------------------------------

### Configure Codegen for Resolvers

Source: https://github.com/dotansimha/graphql-code-generator/blob/master/website/src/pages/docs/guides/graphql-server-apollo-yoga.mdx

Define the codegen configuration in codegen.ts to generate resolver types from your schema.

```typescript
import type { CodegenConfig } from '@graphql-codegen/cli';

const config: CodegenConfig = {
  schema: 'schema.graphql',
  generates: {
    './resolvers-types.ts': {
      config: {
        useIndexSignature: true,
      },
      plugins: ['typescript', 'typescript-resolvers'],
    },
  },
};
export default config;
```

```typescript
import type { CodegenConfig } from '@graphql-codegen/cli';

const config: CodegenConfig = {
  schema: 'schema.graphql',
  generates: {
    './resolvers-types.ts': {
      plugins: ['typescript', 'typescript-resolvers'],
    },
  },
};
export default config;
```

--------------------------------

### Implement Resolvers with Mapped Enums

Source: https://github.com/dotansimha/graphql-code-generator/blob/master/website/src/pages/plugins/typescript/typescript-resolvers.mdx

Usage of the mapped enum within resolver functions.

```typescript
import { ColorsCode } from './enums'
import { Resolvers } from './resolvers-types'

const resolvers: Resolvers = {
  Color: {
    RED: ColorsCode.MY_RED,
    BLUE: ColorsCode.MY_BLUE
  },
  Query: {
    favoriteColor: () => ColorsCode.MY_RED // Now you cn return this, and it will be mapped to your actual GraphQL enum
  }
}
```

--------------------------------

### Define Internal Enum Values

Source: https://github.com/dotansimha/graphql-code-generator/blob/master/website/src/pages/plugins/flow/flow-resolvers.mdx

TypeScript definition for internal enum values used in resolver mapping.

```typescript
export enum ColorsCode {
  MY_RED = '#FF0000',
  MY_BLUE = '#0000FF'
}
```

