### Configure explicit HttpLink in ApolloClient

Source: https://github.com/apollographql/apollo-client/blob/main/docs/source/migrating/apollo-client-4-migration.mdx

Pass an explicit HttpLink instance to ApolloClient's link option instead of the removed top-level uri, headers, and credentials constructor options.

```typescript
import {
  ApolloClient,
  InMemoryCache,
  HttpLink,// [!code ++]
} from "@apollo/client/core";
const client = new ApolloClient({
  // ...
  link: new HttpLink({// [!code ++]
    uri: "https://example.com/graphql",
    credentials: "include",
    headers: { "x-custom-header": "value" },
  }),// [!code ++]
  // ...
});
```

--------------------------------

### Migrate URI, headers, and credentials to HttpLink

Source: https://github.com/apollographql/apollo-client/blob/main/docs/source/migrating/apollo-client-4-migration.mdx

Moves uri, headers, and credentials from ApolloClient options into a new HttpLink instance passed to the link option.

```ts
import { HttpLink } from "@apollo/client"; // [!code ++]

new ApolloClient({
  uri: "/graphql", // [!code --:5]
  credentials: "include",
  headers: {
    "x-custom-header"
  },
  link: new HttpLink({ // [!code ++:6]
    uri: "/graphql",
    credentials: "include",
    headers: {
      "x-custom-header"
    },
  })
})
```

--------------------------------

### Update React hook imports

Source: https://github.com/apollographql/apollo-client/blob/main/docs/source/migrating/apollo-client-4-migration.mdx

Updates React hooks like useQuery from the root package to the @apollo/client/react entry point.

```ts
import { useQuery } from "@apollo/client";// [!code --]
import { useQuery } from "@apollo/client/react";// [!code ++]
```

--------------------------------

### Skip standby queries in client.refetchQueries

Source: https://github.com/apollographql/apollo-client/blob/main/docs/source/migrating/apollo-client-4-migration.mdx

Apollo Client 4 refetches named queries in standby by default. Use the onQueryUpdated callback to check the query fetchPolicy and maintain the Apollo Client 3 behavior of skipping standby queries.

```ts
client.refetchQueries({
  include: ["queryName"],
  onQueryUpdated: (observableQuery) =>
    observableQuery.options.fetchPolicy !== "standby",
});
```

--------------------------------

### Initialize ApolloClient with LocalState

Source: https://github.com/apollographql/apollo-client/blob/main/docs/agent-skills/apollo-client/references/state-management.md

Add LocalState to the ApolloClient initialization to enable support for @client fields in Apollo Client 4.x.

```typescript
import { ApolloClient, InMemoryCache } from "@apollo/client";
import { LocalState } from "@apollo/client/local-state";

const client = new ApolloClient({
  cache: new InMemoryCache(),
  localState: new LocalState({}),
  // ... other options
});
```

